## The Closing

The law of fair trade is not a human invention. It is the ground.

**It existed before we had language. It is the condition of communication. It is the condition of trade. It is the condition of society. It is the condition of survival.**

Communication depends on honest and fair participation. The dialog is a trade. The trade is governed by the law. The law is reciprocity. The reciprocity is the standard. The standard is the ground.

**The ground is the standard. The standard is the truth. The truth is finite. The lies are infinite. The exception is exploitation. The exception is self-negation.**

**The pursuit continues—in fidelity to the ground.**
